{
  "category": "Aqua Rabbit Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "By keeping still and listening intently, it can tell what is in even wild, fast- moving rivers.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it plays in water, it rolls up its elongated ears to prevent their insides from getting wet.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "The bubble-like pattern on its stomach helps it camouflage itself when it's in the water.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "AZUMARILL’s long ears are indispensable sensors. By focusing its hearing, this POKéMON can identify what kinds of prey are around, even in rough and fast-running rivers.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "AZUMARILL can make balloons out of air. It makes these air balloons if it spots a drowning POKéMON. The air balloons enable the POKéMON in trouble to breathe.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives in water virtually all day long. Its body color and pattern act as camouflage that makes it tough for enemies to spot in water.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it plays in water, it rolls up its elongated ears to prevent their insides from getting wet.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "By keeping still and listening intently, it can even tell what is in wild, fast-moving rivers.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives in rivers and lakes. In water, its coloring and patterns trick the vision of foes.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its long ears are superb sensors. It can distinguish the movements of living things on riverbeds.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "It can spend all day in water, since it can inhale and store a large volume of air.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "By keeping still and listening intently, it can tell what is in even wild, fast-moving rivers.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it plays in water, it rolls up its elongated ears to prevent their insides from getting wet.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It can spend all day in water, since it can inhale and store a large volume of air.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "It can spend all day in water, since it can inhale and store a large volume of air.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its long ears are superb sensors. It can distinguish the movements of things in water and tell what they are.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its long ears are superb sensors. It can distinguish the movements of things in water and tell what they are.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its long ears are superb sensors. It can distinguish the movements of living things on riverbeds.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "The bubble-like pattern on its stomach helps it camouflage itself when it’s in the water.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Azumarill’s long ears are indispensable sensors. By focusing its hearing, this Pokémon can identify what kinds of prey are around, even in rough and fast-running rivers.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Azumarill can make balloons out of air. It makes these air balloons if it spots a drowning Pokémon. The air balloons enable the Pokémon in trouble to breathe.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It spends most of its time in the water. On sunny days, Azumarill floats on the surface of the water and sunbathes.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "These Pokémon create air-filled bubbles. When Azurill play in rivers, Azumarill will cover them with these bubbles.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
